    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "figure": "geometric-steps",
      "body": "The nth term of a geometric sequence is a_n = a_1 · r^(n−1): the start times (n − 1) factors of r. For 2, 6, 18, … (a_1 = 2, r = 3), the 4th term is 2 · 3³ = 2 · 27 = 54."
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Use the formula.",
      "predict": {
        "prompt": "aₙ = a₁·rⁿ⁻¹ — why n − 1 in the exponent, not n?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "zero",
            "label": "The first term uses ZERO multiplications"
          },
          {
            "id": "tradition",
            "label": "Off-by-one tradition"
          },
          {
            "id": "size",
            "label": "Because r is bigger than a₁"
          }
        ],
        "outcomeId": "zero",
        "reveal": "a₁ = 2 stands at zero multiplications; every later term adds one ×3. The 4th term has taken 3 jumps: 2·3³ = 54. The exponent counts the JUMPS between terms, not the terms themselves."
      },
      "widget": {
